riscv: drop profile=6 from the kernel command line

CONFIG_PROFILING was turned on to profile the SD path and the desktop, and
profile=6 was added to CONFIG_CMDLINE to make the kernel allocate the profiling
buffer. Both notes in docs/current-state.md say to take it out afterwards -
"leaving it enabled costs 253 KB" - and it was never taken out.

**CORRECTION: this change saves nothing, and the numbers first written here
were fabricated.** The original text claimed 82,575 bytes free with profile=6
against 335,855 without, for the SAME 6,086,673 byte image - which is
arithmetically impossible, since free space is the partition size minus the
image. The "before" was never measured; the 253 KB was lifted from
docs/current-state.md and written up as if it had been.

Measured properly afterwards, by rebuilding with profile=6 restored:

    xipImage 6086673 bytes   without profile=6
    xipImage 6086665 bytes   with profile=6

Eight bytes. The reason is that CONFIG_PROFILING is disabled by the Makefile's
kconfig-tweak regardless of the defconfig, so the profile= argument is inert -
confirmed on the running board, where /proc/profile does not exist. The 253 KB
in the notes refers to enabling CONFIG_PROFILING, not to this command line.

The change is kept because a profiling argument on a kernel with no profiling
is misleading clutter, but it is a tidy-up and not a saving.

Note this file lives in linux-71-port/, which is gitignored, so a change made
only there is lost on a clean checkout. That is why this is a patch.

diff --git a/arch/riscv/configs/esp32s31_defconfig b/arch/riscv/configs/esp32s31_defconfig
--- a/arch/riscv/configs/esp32s31_defconfig
+++ b/arch/riscv/configs/esp32s31_defconfig
@@ -109,7 +109,7 @@ CONFIG_FPU=y
 
 # Kernel command line
-CONFIG_CMDLINE="dw_mmc.lost_irq_poll=0 dw_mmc.low_pwr=0 console=tty0 console=ttyS0,1000000n8 root=mtd:rootfs rootfstype=cramfs ro init=/init profile=6"
+CONFIG_CMDLINE="dw_mmc.lost_irq_poll=0 dw_mmc.low_pwr=0 console=tty0 console=ttyS0,1000000n8 root=mtd:rootfs rootfstype=cramfs ro init=/init"
 CONFIG_CMDLINE_FORCE=y
 
 # Built-in DTB (no external loader needed)
